\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Continuous 2D Bubble Trinity trajectories and discrete local-search mechanism ablation.} \textbf  {(a)} Trajectories of the kernel-induced line energy $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {ind}}(t)$ across $250$ integration steps ($\Delta t = 0.025$) for the four interactive presets of \Cref  {tab:bubble_regimes}, starting from a $4$-swap perturbation of D\"urer's $4\times 4$ square ($\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {ind}}(0) = 1{,}681.89$). Although continuous bubble drift reduces $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {ind}}(t)$ by $37.5\%$, both greedy snapping and exact Hungarian projection fail ($0\%$, $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}\ge 1{,}480$) because $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {ind}}(t)$ relaxes via convex amplitude averaging rather than discrete permutation swaps. \textbf  {(b)} Operator ablation study (\Cref  {tab:physical_analogs_ablation}) contrasting continuous 2D bubble drift and $2$/$3$-exchange heuristics (Tiers~$0\text  {--}2$) against line-preserving $(2,2)$ plaquette moves, candidate-list $(2,2)$ swaps with row/column permutations, thresholded funnel re-anchoring, and multi-restart iterated local search (Tiers~$3\text  {--}6$) at orders $n=4$ ($200$ trials) and $n=5$ ($100$ trials).}}{16}{figure.64}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bubble_trinity}{{6}{16}{\textbf {Continuous 2D Bubble Trinity trajectories and discrete local-search mechanism ablation.} \textbf {(a)} Trajectories of the kernel-induced line energy $\Hind (t)$ across $250$ integration steps ($\Delta t = 0.025$) for the four interactive presets of \Cref {tab:bubble_regimes}, starting from a $4$-swap perturbation of D\"urer's $4\times 4$ square ($\Hind (0) = 1{,}681.89$). Although continuous bubble drift reduces $\Hind (t)$ by $37.5\%$, both greedy snapping and exact Hungarian projection fail ($0\%$, $\Hline \ge 1{,}480$) because $\Hind (t)$ relaxes via convex amplitude averaging rather than discrete permutation swaps. \textbf {(b)} Operator ablation study (\Cref {tab:physical_analogs_ablation}) contrasting continuous 2D bubble drift and $2$/$3$-exchange heuristics (Tiers~$0\text {--}2$) against line-preserving $(2,2)$ plaquette moves, candidate-list $(2,2)$ swaps with row/column permutations, thresholded funnel re-anchoring, and multi-restart iterated local search (Tiers~$3\text {--}6$) at orders $n=4$ ($200$ trials) and $n=5$ ($100$ trials)}{figure.64}{}}
